    "enDesc": "*Kli Yakar* is a Torah commentary by Rabbi Shlomo Ephraim ben Aaron Luntschitz, originally published in 1602. The title, which translates to \"precious jewel,\" is a reference to [Proverbs 20:15](https://www.sefaria.org/Proverbs.20.15?lang=bi&amp;with=all&amp;lang2=en). In the book's introduction, the author writes that he wrote the book as a way of expressing thanks to God after recovering from a harsh illness. *Kli Yakar* focuses on *peshat,* or a straightforward understanding of the biblical text, while also incorporating midrashic texts and engaging with earlier commentaries. Many of the ideas in the commentary are based on weekly sermons that Luntschitz delivered in Lviv and include *musar,* (moral instruction or rebuke), critiquing the pursuit of money and other practices that the author saw as problematic. ",
